Cancelling DisplayDialogComplex: Fast Script Reload - Warning Auto reload for assets/scripts is enabled.

This means any change made in playmode will likely trigger full recompile.

It's an editor setting and can be adjusted at any time via Edit -> Preferences -> Asset Pipeline -> Auto Refresh

I can also adjust that for you now - that means you'll need to manually load changes (outside of playmode) via Assets -> Refresh (CTRL + R).

In some editor versions you can also set script compilation to happen outside of playmode and don't have to manually refresh. 

Depending on version you'll find it via: 
1) Edit -> Preferences -> General -> Script Changes While Playing -> Recompile After Finished Playing.
2) Edit -> Preferences -> Asset Pipeline -> Auto Refresh -> Enabled Outside Playmode
This should not be called in batch mode.
